  <!--
    signer element: defines the expected Authenticode certificate subject
    for independent trust-chain verification.
    
    The subject value must be a substring of the signer certificate's
    Subject Distinguished Name (case-insensitive). It should match the
    hardcoded ExpectedPublisher constant in UpdateService.cs.
    
    When rotating the code-signing certificate, update this element to
    the new subject and also update UpdateService.ExpectedPublisher in
    the same release. See docs/RELEASE.md for the full procedure.

    NOTE: v1.9.0 and v1.9.1 installers are NOT Authenticode-signed (no
    code-signing certificate yet). RequireAuthenticodeSignature defaults
    to false, so updates will proceed in advisory mode.
